 ### Feature cache / query stores
 
+#### Cross-instance attention
+
+`useInstanceAttentionStore.ts` holds one list for every session that needs the
+user, strongest reason first and newest within that. The saved instances the
+poller reads answer from their `/api/session` and `/api/sessions/status` routes,
+plus the routes that say which folders each host opens (`/api/config/settings`,
+`/api/fs/home`, `/api/git/project-worktrees`); while one of them is on screen the
+app's own server answers the same routes under the `local` id. The instance this
+window shows is published by `hooks/useLocalInstanceAttention.ts` as the reserved
+`openchamber:this-instance` entry, derived from
+`sync/global-blocking-requests.ts`, `useGlobalSessionsStore` and
+`sync/session-unread.ts`; a subagent request attributes to its top-level parent.
+A host's folder answer is kept beside its sessions, so a poll that answered its
+sessions but not the folders keeps judging them as before. Every surface reads
+the same `items` array, so the switcher, the phone bell and the collapsed-sidebar
+badge show one total. `retainHosts` keeps the reserved entry because it is never
+in a poller's target list; the `local` entry leaves with the target list when the
+window returns to it.
+
+#### Why the local half loads the session list itself
+
+A host switch resets the global session list (`hasLoaded: false`, no records),
+and the phone mounts no global poller: the list is read again only when the
+sessions sheet opens or the connection reconnects. `hooks/useLocalInstanceAttention.ts`
+therefore reads it when the store holds none, so the instance on screen
+publishes its own waiting sessions right after a switch. Without that read the
+drawer showed only the other saved instances' rows until the sheet was opened,
+which reads as one host having more waiting work than it does.
+
+#### Why the local instance is a store entry and not a second list
+
+A separate local list would make every surface merge two arrays and choose
+between two counts, and the merge would have to repeat the strength order and
+subagent attribution the polled path already owns. Publishing the local half as
+another host entry keeps one derivation and one sorted list; the reserved id is
+the only thing that distinguishes it, and the hook resolves
+`instanceAttention.localInstance` when it publishes, so the row label follows
+the locale instead of storing English in the record.
+
